WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.270
- [Narrator] Hello there.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.130
Oh, hey, watch the road, watch the road.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.340
I just wanted to tell
you a little fun fact.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.810
Did you know that the guy who invented

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:11.160
cruise control couldn't drive?

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.640
He had a good excuse.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:13.583
He was blind.

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:18.248
(playful music)

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.060
This is Ralph Teetor.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.640
He was an amazing guy.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.540
He lost his sight when he was a kid,

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.220
but it didn't slow him down.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.750
He excelled in school

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.690
and became a respected
mechanical engineer.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:35.170
He had a talent for visualizing
objects in his mind.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.090
It led to amazing inventions such as

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.450
an early power lawnmower and a new version

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.670
of the fishing pole.

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:43.603
But his crowning achievement
is cruise control.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.060
The story goes like this.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:49.040
During World War II, the
speed limit was set to 35

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.760
to save on gas and tires.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.400
Teetor's lawyer was driving him around

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.830
and kept having to brake to stay at 35

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.230
and that constant slowing
down and speeding up

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:02.250
started to make our intrepid
inventor feel a little carsick.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:05.980
His blindness made him particularly
sensitive to the motion.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:08.180
An inspiration struck.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:10.090
Ralph came up with an
idea that would control

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.510
the speed of the car without the driver

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:13.200
having to touch the pedals.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.003
Thus, the Speedostat was born.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.710
Obviously, that name didn't catch on.

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:24.350
In 1958, the first car to use
Ralph's invention came out.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.950
At first it was an 86
dollar luxury feature,

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:29.500
but over the years, cruise
control, as it came to be known,

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.210
has become a standard part of most cars.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:34.490
So, the next time that you're
cruisin' down the road,

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:36.360
remember Ralph Teetor.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.893
The genius, the engineer, the visionary.

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:43.897
(playful music)

